--- BUF-01, BUF-05: declaration forms and exact capacity ---
Create a buffer called 'the tray'.
If 'the tray's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'the tray's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's size.
a buffer called 'the register' is 1 bytes.
If 'the register's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'the register's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's size.
If 'the register's capacity is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 1 got {'the register's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's capacity.
a buffer called ledger is 83196 bytes.
If ledger's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {ledger's size}", Exit 95. Print ledger's size.
Print 0 times 0.
If ledger's capacity is not 83196 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 83196 got {ledger's capacity}", Exit 95. Print ledger's capacity.
Print ledger's size.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  Create a buffer called 'the tray',
  If 'the tray's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'the tray's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the tray's size,
  a buffer called 'the register' is 1 bytes,
  If 'the register's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {'the register's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's size,
  If 'the register's capacity is not 1 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 1 got {'the register's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'the register's capacity,
  a buffer called ledger is 83196 bytes,
  If ledger's size is not 0 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-01: expected 0 got {ledger's size}", Exit 95. Print ledger's size,
  Print 0 times 0,
  If ledger's capacity is not 83196 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-05: expected 83196 got {ledger's capacity}", Exit 95. Print ledger's capacity,
  Print ledger's size.

--- BUF-10, BUF-11, BUF-12: size, length, capacity, empty ---
a buffer called 'toolbox' is 7 bytes in size.
If 'toolbox's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'toolbox's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's empty.
append "gtazsxa" to 'toolbox'.
If 'toolbox's size is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size.
If 'toolbox's capacity is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity.
If 'toolbox's length is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 7 got {'toolbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's length.
If 'toolbox's length is not 'toolbox's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'toolbox's size} got {'toolbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's length.
If 'toolbox's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'toolbox's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's empty.
Print 'toolbox's length.

--- the same leaf, nested ---
  a buffer called 'toolbox' is 7 bytes in size,
  If 'toolbox's empty is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 1 got {'toolbox's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's empty,
  append "gtazsxa" to 'toolbox',
  If 'toolbox's size is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'toolbox's size}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's size,
  If 'toolbox's capacity is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-10: expected 7 got {'toolbox's capacity}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's capacity,
  If 'toolbox's length is not 7 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected 7 got {'toolbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's length,
  If 'toolbox's length is not 'toolbox's size then, Print "ASSERT BUF-11: expected {'toolbox's size} got {'toolbox's length}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's length,
  If 'toolbox's empty then, Print "ASSERT BUF-12: expected 0 got {'toolbox's empty}", Exit 95. Print 'toolbox's empty,
  Print 'toolbox's length.

--- BUF-13: full, filled to capacity exactly ---
a buffer called workbench is 73 bytes in size.
If workbench's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {workbench's full}", Exit 95. Print workbench's full.
append "0lyb0hafw9q3o12bw5evkdm341mf09qbc9mfw5qzohi3k5ez816vgdy3clifotirw9ebwl6j" to workbench.
If workbench's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {workbench's full}", Exit 95. Print workbench's full.
append "c" to workbench.
If workbench's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {workbench's full}", Exit 95. Print workbench's full.
If workbench's size is not 73 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 73 got {workbench's size}", Exit 95. Print workbench's size.
Print workbench's size.

--- BUF-13 again, a different split and a dynamic buffer ---
a buffer called 'the sketchpad' is 23 bytes in size.
If 'the sketchpad's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's full.
append "un412bgtuf8tij0tano9i" to 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's full.
append "k" to 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's full then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 0 got {'the sketchpad's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's full.
append "9" to 'the sketchpad'.
If 'the sketchpad's full is false then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 1 got {'the sketchpad's full}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's full.
If 'the sketchpad's size is not 23 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-13: expected 23 got {'the sketchpad's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the sketchpad's size.
a buffer called 'notebook'.
append "7s1efkpu7k5izw1yngd2v85" to 'notebook'.
Print 'notebook's full.
Print 'the sketchpad's size.

--- BUF-03: dynamic growth past the reserve ---
a buffer called 'the crate'.
a number called 'the crate appends made' is 0.
a boolean called 'the crate overflowed' is false.
a boolean called 'the crate found an error already pending' is false.
On error Set 'the crate found an error already pending' to true.
While 'the crate appends made' is less than 269, append "vgp6fcdab41qfwtuv0leno9qr0x6fo" to 'the crate', On error Set 'the crate overflowed' to true. Set 'the crate appends made' to 'the crate appends made' add 1.
If 'the crate's size is not 8070 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 8070 got {'the crate's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the crate's size.
If 'the crate overflowed' then, Print "ASSERT BUF-03: expected 0 got {'the crate overflowed'}", Exit 95. Print 'the crate overflowed'.
Print 'the crate's size.

--- BUF-07: a read that truncates, detected by size ---
a text called 'the tally sheet path' is "{'the workspace'}/buffer1".
open a file for writing called 'the tally sheet being written' at 'the tally sheet path'.
Write "oxibgx6b0xa7ktyzsp2fo1efsdm7wdyv0xmzclqb41y3glangtej4xmf4tqrgt6z4dyb0tirstujctynsdmfcd2j81uzshejw1u3cdunsdqfspqjo1" to 'the tally sheet being written'.
Close 'the tally sheet being written'.
open a file for reading called 'the tally sheet being read' at 'the tally sheet path'.
a buffer called 'the tally sheet' is 22 bytes in size.
a boolean called 'the tally sheet was truncated' is false.
Read from 'the tally sheet being read' into 'the tally sheet'.
On error Set 'the tally sheet was truncated' to true.
Close 'the tally sheet being read'.
If 'the tally sheet's size is not 22 then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected 22 got {'the tally sheet's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the tally sheet's size.
If 'the tally sheet's size is not 'the tally sheet's capacity then, Print "ASSERT BUF-07: expected {'the tally sheet's capacity} got {'the tally sheet's size}", Exit 95. Print 'the tally sheet's size.
Print 'the tally sheet's size.

